{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [Unnumbered location plan, KAMARAN/PLAN/001, KAMARAN/PLAN/002, KAMARAN/PLAN/003. Received 23/01/2025].\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - No additional windows or openings shall be formed in the side elevation of the development hereby permitted.\r\nReason: In order to protect neighbours' privacy.\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - Within one planting season of the removal of the tree located close to the western boundary treatment, a replacement tree shall be replanted as near to the location of the felled tree as possible. The tree shall be of  'Standard' size i.e. with a single stem with clear trunk at least 1.8 metres and a girth of not less than 8-10 centimetres at a point one metre above ground level at the time of planting and shall be maintained in perpetuity. Should a replacement tree die or become seriously damaged or moribund, then a further replacement tree to the same specification shall be planted immediately.\r\nReason: In order to maintain the character and appearance of this site and the character and appearance of the wider area in which it sits.",
    "Condition : 5 - Prior to occupation of the extension hereby approved, evidence shall have been submitted to the local planning authority for approval in writing to demonstrate that the premises has been fitted out to a specified internal noise insulation level above that required by British Standard BS8233:2014 and/or its subsequent amendments, so as to provide sound insulation against sudden and underlying noise generated by the approved development which might affect residential units located above or to the sides of the site. The site shall be used in such a manner as to ensure that the noise insulation measures so approved are effective at all times.\r\nReason: In order to protect neighbours' living conditions."
  ],
